# Ent Schema Definition

## 1. Schema Structure

Schemas are defined in `ent/schema` and must embed `ent.Schema`.

```go
package schema

import (
    "entgo.io/ent"
    "entgo.io/ent/schema/field"
    "entgo.io/ent/schema/edge"
)

type User struct {
    ent.Schema
}

func (User) Fields() []ent.Field {
    return []ent.Field{
        field.String("name").NotEmpty(),
        field.Int("age").Positive(),
    }
}

func (User) Edges() []ent.Edge {
    return []ent.Edge{
        edge.To("pets", Pet.Type),
    }
}
```

## 2. Fields

Use `field.<Type>` to define fields. Chain validators and modifiers.

### Common Types
- `field.String`, `field.Int`, `field.Bool`, `field.Time`
- `field.UUID`, `field.JSON`, `field.Enum`

### Modifiers
- `.Default(value)`
- `.Optional()` (nullable)
- `.Unique()`
- `.Immutable()` (cannot be updated)
- `.Sensitive()` (omitted from String/JSON)
- `.StructTag("json: \"custom_name\"")`

### Example
```go
field.String("email").
    Unique().
    NotEmpty().
    MaxLen(255)
```

## 3. Edges (Relationships)

Define relationships between entities.

### Types
- **O2O (One-to-One):** `edge.To("card", Card.Type).Unique()` (and back `edge.From(...).Unique()`)
- **O2M (One-to-Many):** `edge.To("pets", Pet.Type)` (and back `edge.From("owner", User.Type).Ref("pets").Unique()`)
- **M2M (Many-to-Many):** `edge.To("groups", Group.Type)` (and back `edge.From("users", User.Type).Ref("groups")`)

### Inverse Edges (Back-references)
ALWAYS define inverse edges for bidirectional navigation. Use `.Ref()` on the "child" side.

```go
// User (Parent)
func (User) Edges() []ent.Edge {
    return []ent.Edge{
        edge.To("pets", Pet.Type),
    }
}

// Pet (Child)
func (Pet) Edges() []ent.Edge {
    return []ent.Edge{
        edge.From("owner", User.Type).
            Ref("pets").
            Unique().
            Required(),
    }
}
```

## 4. Indexes

Define database indexes for performance or uniqueness constraints on multiple fields.

```go
func (User) Indexes() []ent.Index {
    return []ent.Index{
        index.Fields("name", "age").
            Unique(),
    }
}
```

## 5. Mixins

Reuse schema parts (fields, edges, hooks) across multiple schemas.

```go
// ent/schema/mixin.go
type TimeMixin struct {
    mixin.Schema
}

func (TimeMixin) Fields() []ent.Field {
    return []ent.Field{
        field.Time("created_at").Default(time.Now).Immutable(),
        field.Time("updated_at").Default(time.Now).UpdateDefault(time.Now),
    }
}

// ent/schema/user.go
func (User) Mixin() []ent.Mixin {
    return []ent.Mixin{
        TimeMixin{},
    }
}
```

## 6. Annotations

Customize storage or generation.

```go
func (User) Annotations() []schema.Annotation {
    return []schema.Annotation{
        entsql.Annotation{Table: "users_custom_table"},
    }
}
```

